@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il27-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il27-tax-years`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance s 40B — "נקודת זיכוי לנער". Row IL-27. Source lines 1651-1652.
--
-- One credit point for an individual who, or whose spouse, has completed 16 years but not 18.
--
-- ONE POINT. "תובא בחשבון נקודת זיכוי" is one point: it is one point whether the individual, the spouse or both are of that age.
-- AGE. A person has completed n years on the day of his nth birthday. At what time in the tax year the age is measured, the text does
-- not say (fork F4): on its last day; on some day; or on every day. RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): one named switch, default
-- declined where the three give different answers, which they do for one who turns 16 or 18 in the year. The three agree for one who
-- is 16 or 17 throughout the year, and for one who is far from both.
-- Fork F1 (residence) applies: the section names none.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 40B — credit for a youth`

-- src:1652 | בחישוב המס של יחיד שמלאו לו או לבן־זוגו 16 שנים אך לא 18 שנים תובא בחשבון נקודת זיכוי.

-- Completed years of one born on `born`, on `day`: the years between, less one if the birthday has not come yet.
@ref ITO s 40B, line 1652
GIVEN born IS A DATE
      day  IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the age of one born on` born `, on` day MEANS
    DATE_YEAR day MINUS DATE_YEAR born
    MINUS (IF DATE_MONTH day TIMES 100 PLUS DATE_DAY day LESS THAN DATE_MONTH born TIMES 100 PLUS DATE_DAY born THEN 1 ELSE 0)

GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40B — an age of 16 years or more but not 18:` age MEANS
    age AT LEAST 16 AND age LESS THAN 18

@ref ITO s 40B, line 1652; fork F4
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 40B does not say when in the tax year the age is measured, and here the readings differ` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 40B does not say when in the tax year the age is measured, and here the readings differ"

@ref ITO s 40B, line 1652; fork F4
GIVEN born IS A DATE
      `the year` IS A NUMBER
      r IS A `A reading of "has completed 16 years but not 18" in section 40B`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`one born on` born `is of the age of section 40B in tax year` `the year` `, reading the age as` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `on the last day of the tax year` THEN `last`
    WHEN `on some day of the tax year`     THEN `some`
    WHEN `on every day of the tax year`    THEN `every`
    WHEN `declined where the readings differ`
        THEN IF   `last` EQUALS `some` AND `some` EQUALS `every`
             THEN `last`
             ELSE `section 40B does not say when in the tax year the age is measured, and here the readings differ`
    WHERE
        `at the start` MEANS `the age of one born on` born `, on` (YMD `the year` 1 1)
        `at the end`   MEANS `the age of one born on` born `, on` (YMD `the year` 12 31)
        `last`  MEANS `s 40B — an age of 16 years or more but not 18:` `at the end`
        `some`  MEANS `at the end` AT LEAST 16 AND `at the start` LESS THAN 18
        `every` MEANS `at the start` AT LEAST 16 AND `at the end` LESS THAN 18

@ref ITO s 40B, line 1652; fork F4
GIVETH A `A reading of "has completed 16 years but not 18" in section 40B`
`section 40B — the reading row IL-27 takes of the age` MEANS
    `declined where the readings differ`

@ref ITO s 40B, line 1652; forks F1, F4
GIVEN ra IS A `A reading of "has completed 16 years but not 18" in section 40B`
      rr IS A `A reading of the sections that name no residence condition (ss 39A, 39B, 40A, 40B)`
      i  IS AN `An individual and a spouse, for section 40B`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 40B, reading the age as` ra `and the residence condition as` rr `, for` i MEANS
    `for tax year` (i's `tax year`) `, row IL-27 answers`
        (`the points, unless section 48A may take them from a foreign worker:` (i's `a foreign worker`) `,`
            (`points under a section that names no residence condition, for` (i's `an Israeli resident in the tax year`) `, the points being` `the points` `, reading the condition as` rr))
    WHERE
        `the year`       MEANS i's `tax year`
        `individual is`  MEANS `one born on` (i's `date of birth of the individual`) `is of the age of section 40B in tax year` `the year` `, reading the age as` ra
        `the points`     MEANS
            CONSIDER i's `date of birth of the spouse`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN IF `individual is` THEN 1 ELSE 0
            WHEN JUST d THEN
                IF   `individual is` OR `one born on` d `is of the age of section 40B in tax year` `the year` `, reading the age as` ra
                THEN 1
                ELSE 0

@export The credit points under Income Tax Ordinance s 40B (an individual, or a spouse, who has completed 16 years but not 18) for a tax year from 2024: one point, however many of the two are of that age; declines where the age depends on when in the year it is measured, for one who is not an Israeli resident, and for a foreign worker (s 48A)
@ref ITO s 40B, lines 1651-1652
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual and a spouse, for section 40B`
          @desc the tax year, residence, the dates of birth of the individual and of the spouse (if any)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 40B for` i MEANS
    `the credit points under section 40B, reading the age as` `section 40B — the reading row IL-27 takes of the age` `and the residence condition as` `the reading row IL-27 takes of the sections that name no residence condition` `, for` i
